Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:30:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): [daveey] paint a clicked session's cached
 transcript in the click

Live [open-timing] (2026-10-28): cache paints took 112-154 ms from the click,
local and hub alike, and warm reopens (no cache read) 82-86 ms, while a
resume with no click painted from cache in 13 ms. So ~85-100 ms of every
open sat between the click and resumeSession: opening into main routes
first and resumes in the route effect, after React renders the route change.

The sidebar click now paints the row's cached transcript itself
(prepaintClickedTranscript), so the rows commit with the route change. Only
when the click loads main: a session already selected or open as a tile is
focused, an asleep row keeps its read-only open. The resume repaints the same
rows from the same scope, display-only as before; the click's paint is the
one [open-timing] records.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
